;; M4S import-then-edit (docs/m4s-contract.md, required fixtures): the
;; m5-keep shape over a would-be-admissible cone -- plain tables + one
;; struct relation, single acyclic stratum, NO lattice anywhere (unlike
;; base2_input, whose dist/cost keeps the program outside M4S admission).
;; The session imports a frozen mini bin-db asserting (out (pair 7 8))
;; directly; nothing re-derives it, so its liveness -- and the struct
;; row's foundation -- must come from the input ledger (the payload's
;; struct heap is recorded as direct input exactly like its table rows).
;;
;; With in = {(1,2), (3,4)} plus the import:
;;   out  = { (pair 1 2) (pair 3 4) (pair 7 8) }
;;   pair (1 2)/(3 4) -> (input 0, nonrec 1, rec 0)   constructed
;;   pair (7 8)       -> (input 1, nonrec 0, rec 0)   ledger foundation
;;   out  (pair 7 8)  -> (input 1, nonrec 0, rec 0)
;; Deleting in(3,4) removes exactly out/pair (3 4); the imported row's
;; embedded id must stay valid across settlement.

struct (pair int int)
table (in int int)
table (out pair)

rule
(in X Y)
-->
(out (pair X Y))
